# {{ name }}

<!-- One line: the job this frontend does, and for whom. -->

A front end for one job. It runs on its own as an app, and ships
cards that a dashboard app's dashboard shows. It keeps no data;
{%- if backend == 'new' %} its backend is a backend (a Django API) at `VITE_API_URL`.
{%- else %} its backend is an existing system at `VITE_API_URL`, which keeps its own data and sign-in.
{%- endif %}

## Run

```sh
npm ci
cp .env.example .env
npm run dev
```

`npm run build` writes `dist/`: the app, and the cards at `dist/embed/`.

## Settings

Read in `src/config.ts`. Unset optional settings turn their feature off.

| Setting | Default | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `VITE_API_URL` | none, required | Base URL of the backend. |{% if backend == 'existing' %}
| `VITE_SIGNIN_URL` | none | The system's login page; the return address is appended. Odoo: `https://<host>/web/login?redirect=`. The frontend must be on the same registrable domain as the system (CONTRACT.md, "Same site"). |{% endif %}
| `VITE_NAV_SRC` | none | Script URL of the dashboard app's nav. Set: the nav replaces this app's top bar. |
| `VITE_NAV_TAG` | `site-nav` | Tag name the nav script defines. |
| `VITE_THEME_CSS` | none | The dashboard app's stylesheet of `--theme-*` variables, loaded after this app's CSS. |

## Cards

Served at `/embed/{{ slug }}.js` (it loads `/embed/kit.js` beside it).

| Tag | Attributes | Shows |
|---|---|---|
| `<{{ slug }}-items>` | `data-up` (backend base URL), `data-org` (org slug), `data-app` (this app's URL, for the link) | The org's items. Hidden when there are none or the viewer cannot see them. |

## Links

URL shapes of this app. Once listed here, a shape is never removed or reshaped; it
only gains redirects.

| Shape | Shows |
|---|---|
| `/` | Your orgs; with one, straight to it. |
| `/o/<org>/` | That org's items. Cards expand here. |

